{"availability":"available","full":"Landfall-ST/landfall","name":"landfall","description":"Independent, ledger-derived settlement intelligence for Stellar anchors  know if the money landed before a wallet routes a payment.","category":"Finance","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-05T17:22:32Z","updated":"2026-10-08T20:24:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://landfall-chi.vercel.app","topics":["anchor","blockchain","developer-tools","fintech","payments","soroban","stellar","stellar-blockchain"],"demo":"https://landfall-chi.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.016Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.016Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.016Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.016Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Independent settlement intelligence for Stellar — evidence about a counterparty, computed from the public ledger rather than supplied by the counterparty.","Every answer to that question available today comes from the party being assessed: their stellar.toml, their /info endpoint, their status page. Each is editable in ten seconds. Landfall does not ask them. It reads what their accounts actually did on-chain, and publishes the result permissionlessly — for anchors, for arbitrary addresses, and for the payee an autonomous agent is about to sign a payment to.","What it will not do: move your money. Landfall holds no keys, signs no payments, and takes no custody — every step that moves value belongs to the wallet or the anchor. That is a standing design decision, not a missing feature (why)."],"features":["SEP-1 resolves a home domain to the accounts an anchor claims to operate — permissionlessly, with no cooperation required.","SEP-24 puts one leg of every deposit and withdrawal on the public ledger, so settlement behaviour is already there, retroactively, for every anchor — a prober starts collecting the day you switch it on, Landfall…","CAP-67 (Protocol 23) turns per-account paging into one unified event stream, and makes mint/burn distinguishable from transfer instead of inferred.","SEP-38 firm quotes give slippage — quoted amount versus landed amount — a defined baseline, which nothing in the ecosystem publishes today.","x402 turns \"can an agent pay?\" into a solved problem, and leaves \"who should an agent pay?\" open — see below."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Landfall-ST/landfall/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8ee674e2b0118f1b904725ef8f7dc9e6ec5e78101c9df8855cb2d95146aff641","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.869Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.183Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Independent settlement intelligence for Stellar — evidence about a counterparty, computed from the public ledger rather than supplied by the counterparty.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Landfall-ST/landfall/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"SEP-1 resolves a home domain to the accounts an anchor claims to operate — permissionlessly, with no cooperation required.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Landfall-ST/landfall/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"Brings up a local Stellar Quickstart node, Postgres with the schema applied, the indexer, and the API — no account anywhere, no mainnet, no credentials.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Landfall-ST/landfall/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8ee674e2b0118f1b904725ef8f7dc9e6ec5e78101c9df8855cb2d95146aff641","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Landfall-ST/landfall/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.183Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T20:24:29Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Landfall-ST/landfall/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:18.184Z","hash":"8ee674e2b0118f1b904725ef8f7dc9e6ec5e78101c9df8855cb2